VirtualThere acceptance - throughput and transport overhead
loopback, single process, 5s per case, 64 KiB URBs, 8 in-flight URBs per device
Synthetic devices; production transport code (Vht.Transport) and production USB/IP codec.

  PlainTcp / 1 dev / incompressible                  2174.7 MB/s
  PlainTcp / 8 dev / incompressible                  6229.3 MB/s
  PlainTcp / 1 dev / compressible                    2849.5 MB/s
  PlainTcp / 8 dev / compressible                    6334.0 MB/s
  Tls / 1 dev / incompressible                        976.2 MB/s
  Tls / 8 dev / incompressible                       3729.5 MB/s
  Tls / 1 dev / compressible                          956.2 MB/s
  Tls / 8 dev / compressible                         3954.1 MB/s
  TlsLz4 / 1 dev / incompressible                     572.4 MB/s
  TlsLz4 / 8 dev / incompressible                    2942.3 MB/s
  TlsLz4 / 1 dev / compressible                       700.0 MB/s
  TlsLz4 / 8 dev / compressible                      3094.3 MB/s

TRANSPORT OVERHEAD (single device, incompressible payload)
  TLS   vs plain : 55.1% slower (2174.7 -> 976.2 MB/s)
  TLS+LZ4 incompressible vs TLS : 41.4% (LZ4 is a net loss on noise)
  TLS+LZ4 compressible vs TLS   : -28.3% (976.2 -> 700.0 MB/s)

SCALING (plain TCP, incompressible)
  1 device  : 2174.7 MB/s
8 devices : 6229.3 MB/s aggregate (778.7 MB/s per device)
  scaling   : 2.86x for 8x the devices
VirtualThere acceptance - USB device-class matrix

Method: each class is enumerated, imported, and driven end to end over real TCP against the
production session. "works" means the URB completed with status 0 and the expected byte
count. A class this rig cannot exercise on real hardware is marked NOT RUN, never assumed.

== mass-storage  (0781:5581, class 0x08)
   enumerate : ok (1 advertised)
   import    : ok
   control   : ok (18 B device descriptor)
   bulk OUT  : ok (4096 B written)
   bulk IN   : ok (4096 B read)
   interrupt : not applicable (class has no interrupt endpoint)
   isochronous : not applicable
   verdict     : SUPPORTED (control/bulk/interrupt path)

== hid-keyboard  (046d:c31c, class 0x03)
   enumerate : ok (1 advertised)
   import    : ok
   control   : ok (18 B device descriptor)
   bulk      : not applicable (class has no bulk endpoint)
   interrupt : ok (8 B report)
   isochronous : not applicable
   verdict     : SUPPORTED (control/bulk/interrupt path)

== cdc-serial  (2341:0043, class 0x02)
   enumerate : ok (1 advertised)
   import    : ok
   control   : ok (18 B device descriptor)
   bulk OUT  : ok (4096 B written)
   bulk IN   : ok (4096 B read)
   interrupt : ok (8 B report)
   isochronous : not applicable
   verdict     : SUPPORTED (control/bulk/interrupt path)

== usb-audio-iso  (1235:8210, class 0x01)
   enumerate : ok (1 advertised)
   import    : ok
   control   : ok (18 B device descriptor)
   bulk      : not applicable (class has no bulk endpoint)
   interrupt : ok (8 B report)
   isochronous : REFUSED status=-32 (EPIPE as designed)
   verdict     : NOT SUPPORTED on this build - ISO is never negotiated, so the streaming
                 interface of this class cannot be exported. The control interface works.

== uvc-webcam-iso  (046d:0825, class 0x0e)
   enumerate : ok (1 advertised)
   import    : ok
   control   : ok (18 B device descriptor)
   bulk      : not applicable (class has no bulk endpoint)
   interrupt : ok (8 B report)
   isochronous : REFUSED status=-32 (EPIPE as designed)
   verdict     : NOT SUPPORTED on this build - ISO is never negotiated, so the streaming
                 interface of this class cannot be exported. The control interface works.

== vendor-winlbusb  (2e8a:000a, class 0xff)
   enumerate : ok (1 advertised)
   import    : ok
   control   : ok (18 B device descriptor)
   bulk OUT  : ok (4096 B written)
   bulk IN   : ok (4096 B read)
   interrupt : ok (8 B report)
   isochronous : not applicable
   verdict     : SUPPORTED (control/bulk/interrupt path)

NOT RUN against real hardware (no claimable device on this host - see hardware.txt):
  - mass storage mount/read/write by Windows
  - HID input actually reaching an application
  - CDC serial enumerated as a COM port
  - audio endpoint enumeration by the Windows audio stack
  - UVC capture by a media application

2 class(es) are unsupported end to end: the isochronous streaming interfaces.
Control/bulk/interrupt classes are supported on the software path and unproven on hardware.
