--- C. the structural invariant ----------------------------------------------
  tests/Vht.Core.Tests/BindStatusInvariantTests.cs reflects over Vht.Core.BindStatus and
  fails the build if a member matching Max.*Devices or Device.*Limit ever appears. That test
  is part of the normal test run and is the enforcement mechanism for this claim.

VERDICT
  binary vocabulary occurrences : 6 (quoted above, all classified)
  enforcement-shaped occurrences: 0
  PASS - no licence/device-cap vocabulary exists in any shipped binary in a form that
  reads as a gate. Every occurrence is the product SAYING it has no such gate:
  'device limit: null (no cap)', 'licence: ...', 'nothing here is licensed or capped'.
  The claim this card has to prove is narrower than 'the words never appear': it is that no
  code path can REFUSE an export or an attach because of a licence or a device count.
  That is proven positively by multi.txt (K concurrent devices, none refused) and negatively
  by the classification above. Both are attached verbatim.
